{"name":"Safari Map","hex":"#e2ccba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safari","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip into any undeveloped area to see, photograph or to hunt wild animals in their own environment.","A caravan going on a safari."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a safari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safari"},{"term":"map","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Austronesian languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A visual representation of an area, whether real or imaginary, showing the relative positions of places and other features.","A graphical or logical representation of any structure or system, showing the positions of or relationships between its components."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/map"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safari","blocks":[{"text":"A safari is an overland journey to observe or hunt wild animals, especially in East Africa. The so-called \"Big Five\" game animals of Africa – lion, leopard, rhinoceros, elephant, and Cape buffalo – particularly form an important part of the safari market, both for wildlife viewing and big-game hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg/330px-Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari"},{"title":"Map","blocks":[{"text":"In cartography, a map is a representation or abstraction of geographic reality. Maps are used for a wide range of purposes, including navigation, scientific research, governance, and warfare. A common use is route planning, which enables users to find their way to their destination. Specialized maps called charts are used for nautical navigation and aviation. Scientists use maps to organize spatial data in fields such as geology, meteorology, seismology and demographics. Governments use maps for administrative functions such as census, electoral districts, property taxation, dispatching police, and coordinating disaster relief. Military and security organizations use maps for mission planning, surveillance, border management, logistics, and intelligence analysis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/World_Map_1689.JPG/330px-World_Map_1689.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Map"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ernest Hemingway posing with a Cape buffalo he shot on a safari hunt in Africa in the early 1950s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErnest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg/330px-Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg/330px-Charles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man in safari gear in the early 1900s","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Wellington_Furlong.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Puerto_Rico-VI_TAC.pdf/page1-500px-Puerto_Rico-VI_TAC.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co